\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s it!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted. Below, in the leech lake, two leechmen tried to force the ox\u8217\'92s snout into a bag of freeweed smoke. \u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s IT!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rushed to the edge of the patio. His eyes flew wide when the yellow-headed ox bucked both leechmen off its back. With another hip-shift and buck, the ox broke its constraints, then jumped its rail. The beast tore through the leech lake, kicking up waves of confused, copulating leeches.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Stop that ox!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted as he pointed with his loaded brush. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s three silver-strings of leeches attached to that beast! If you don\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Lora moaned from her seat. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re rich already. You don\u8217\'92t need the money from another bundle of leeches. Let it go.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t ask me to let go of my principles,\u8221\'94 Vigram replied. \u8220\'93That beast is MINE!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stomped back towards the canvas. He set his brush down on the palette, not caring that it rolled into a swatch of blue. Ever the man of action, he marched down to the leech lakes to slap his lazy leechmen. He ordered them after the ox. He screamed at them, bald head rumpling, but his screaming only worked against him, for it stirred a few bleeding cows and goats out of their drug induced reverie. Their horrid shrieks woke up others, and they shrieked too, a cascade of tortured screams. Vigram threw his head back and yelled right back at them. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He\u8217\'92ll be better for it,\u8221\'94 Lora said as she slid off her stool. \u8220\'93He has to let it out once in a while.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You say you\u8217\'92re his }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 niece}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 ?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Mandri asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora smiled as she sauntered over to the easel. Her intrepid hand brushed the back of Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s arm. \u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t like him either, if that\u8217\'92s what you\u8217\'92re wondering. Now, let me see what he has\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 oh wow\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Her portrait looked like her face had been painted onto an apple, then run over by a cartwheel.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It could be better,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93I think it\u8217\'92s the hands.\u8221\'94 He stepped forward to make a play at correcting them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora sidled forward with him, stifling a laugh. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He\u8217\'92s turned me into a demon!\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s not only the hands\u8230\'85though they do look like claws.\u8221\'94 She grabbed Mandri\u8217\'92s own hand and gave it a squeeze. \u8220\'93Artists need strong and dexterous hands, don\u8217\'92t they?\u8221\'94 She smiled, tried to catch him staring.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uh\u8230\'85no\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Mandri stammered. \u8220\'93Well, yes, but, uh\u8230\'85 I don\u8217\'92t have any, uh, dexterity. I actually haven\u8217\'92t painted anything in years.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri tore himself away from her grip. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s too expensive,\u8221\'94 he said instinctively. \u8220\'93Look at all this pigment. The canvas. It would take me weeks to afford all of this. Your uncle makes this in half a finger.\u8221\'94 He scraped a slap of yellow ochre back into its little clay jar. There was enough untouched pigment left on the palette for at least four more of these awkward lessons.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, listen to me,\u8221\'94 Lora said, demanding, causing him to fumble with the jar of paint. \u8220\'93Vigram doesn\u8217\'92t care about these lessons. The only reason you are here today is so that I can get to know you, so stop avoiding me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m not avoiding you it\u8217\'92s just\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 wait, why would you want to get to know me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Because I\u8217\'92m looking for someone, and I think there\u8217\'92s good chance that someone is you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri-__ \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Lora,\u8221\'94 he said, \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re a beautiful girl, but I\u8217\'92m sorry, I\u8217\'92m not available.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes you are.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No, you don\u8217\'92t understand. I don\u8217\'92t want anything to do with anyone.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Good,\u8221\'94 Lora said. \u8220\'93I find that attractive.\u8221\'94 An easy smile played on her lips. or the blunt demeanor, was a sudden ; Mandri no longer saw a girl trained in the art of woman-standing-still, he saw a person. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Specifically, I\u8217\'92m looking for resentment,\u8221\'94 Lora said. \u8220\'93When someone looks a certain way, unkempt, it\u8217\'92s irresistible. The more a man resents himself and his place in the world, the more likely I am to notice him. Unkempt. Falling apart. Does that sound like you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t think of himself as unkempt. He hadn\u8217\'92t shaved in weeks and his robes might be fraying at the sleeves, but, well, anyways, she didn\u8217\'92t know a damned thing about him.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m sorry,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t understand what\u8217\'92s happening here.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re a thin veneer lidding a black pit of shame.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What are you, a wannabe poet?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t worry Mandri, that\u8217\'92s exactly my type.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Shame? That\u8217\'92s what you look for in a man?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It is. Shame; sadness; exhaustion. The more the better.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora picked up Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s paintbrush and rolled it\u8217\'92s handle between her fingers. Her sly, expectant look pricked Mandri\u8217\'92s skin. She asked, \u8220\'93Have you ever been seduced?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is that what\u8217\'92s happening here?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll be more direct: are you still tethered to your flesh?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I suppose I\u8217\'92ll be even more direct.\u8221\'94 She stepped forward, into Mandri\u8217\'92s comfort zone, and closer still. Animal fear, kissing distance. She was about an eyebrow shorter than him, but a whole lot thicker. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Touch me,\u8221\'94 she said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why?\u8221\'94 Mandri mumbled.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora laughed and grabbed Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s arm to pull him into a squeeze. She caught his eyes, forced him to confront her lilac scent, her pounding heat, her smooth skin, her honeyed, aching lips.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Lora\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Mandri muttered. He knew he had to be very careful here. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re a beautiful girl, but\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But what? You go in for men?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No, I just don\u8217\'92t understand what is going on here.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Have you never had fun before? You should try, I think it would be good for you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93And what do you get out of it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s inviting smile widened. Her warmth overwhelmed. The soft shadows of the vines overhead framed her hazel eyes with the most magnificent golden light\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 a magical vesture indeed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She leaned in.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Her gentle lips parted just shy of his cheek.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll get the end of the world,\u8221\'94 she said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Her breath prickled his skin. And now he was on the precipice. His hand gripped her waist, ostensibly to push her away, but her brown robe was so very thin, and the heat of her, intense. Coupled with the curve of her figure, it was almost enough to make him forget that this was a total stranger who, by natural law, should find him repulsive. And more than that, this was not what he was here for.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 A loud grunt drew his gaze to the trellis behind Lora\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s flower-studded curls. In between the diamond gaps of wood and leafy vine, he glimpsed that giant yellow-headed ox hurtling towards them both. The lower half of its body was covered in swinging leeches.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Watch out!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He shoved Lora out of the way.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He dove aside himself.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The old ox, sagging spine and all, rammed right through the trellis, sending a shower of wood splinters onto the patio. Dewlap flapping, it crashed into Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s easel. Several foot long leeches flew through the air.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93MRRRRUUUUUUUUUU!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s wheeling hooves scratched and slipped on the brick. After a moment of chaos, it steadied itself, legs wide like a water bug, and then it bucked into the opposite side of the trellis. It broke through, scraped a few more leeches off its haunches, then disappeared into the marshgrass.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stormed back out onto the patio. His head was red and sweaty. His chest, panting. His eyes darted between Lora, who lay sprawled on the floor, Mandri, who was much the same, and his abandoned painting, which lay face down on the dirty brick. Two little leeches wiggled on top of the frame. Then his wild gaze seized upon the ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s shaved rump as it bounced through the grass. His jaw dropped. His eyes widened. He transcended the bounds of anger, peaking into pure amazement, like he\u8217\'92d just heard an upstart beggar claim to be god, only to find out, the rascal was.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You tempted him? I missed it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We were interrupted.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m apologize. Deeply. Agh, the ox was,}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram, calm yourself.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see Fate!\u8221\'94 Vigram declared.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri brushed the dirt off the skirt of his robe. He stood up. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m leaving,\u8221\'94 he said firmly. He was still bewildered by Lora\u8217\'92s advance, and the ox\u8217\'92s intrusion, and now, Vigram\u8217\'92s rapturous mood. Against all this, he dared to hold out his hand, upturned\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8220\'93If you could pay me my money, that would be great.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, calm yourself,\u8221\'94 Lora said. All the girlish charm in her voice had vanished. "Not every interruption is a scheme of Fate.\u8221\'94 Stern and measured, she stood up and fixed her hair. She smiled at Mandri\u8217\'92s demanding hand like it was cute. \u8220\'93He is not as empty inside as you claimed,\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93Not only did he succumb to temptation, but he desired to protect himself from injury. He desires life.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What, because he dodged the ox\u8217\'92s charge? I addressed this before\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 we should not mistake any acts of self-preservation for vitality. He is a broken young man, I assure you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m sorry,\u8221\'94 Mandri interjected, still holding out his hand. \u8220\'93What is happening here?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram chuckled, then stroked his beard. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She was a test to determine how tethered you were to your flesh.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You were seduced,\u8221\'94 Lora added.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Seduced?\u8221\'94 Mandri scoffed. \u8220\'93Is that what you were trying to do? I didn\u8217\'92t notice. You should try stuffing your tits.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You see!?\u8221\'94 Vigram exclaimed. \u8220\'93The moment he learns your interest in him was a ruse, he moves to mock you. He cannot bear the thought that he was taken advantage of, made a fool. See the way he stands. I should say that the boy is nothing more than a thin veneer lidding a black pit of shame. I say, he is exactly what we need! Look at him! He }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 is}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  empty!\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He is common,\u8221\'94 Lora intoned. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But the ox! You never truly kissed!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora gave Vigram a considerate frown. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I suppose it could be called an auspicious moment.\u8221\'94 She eyed Mandri as though appraising a slave. \u8220\'93I shall query his Fate again.\u8221\'94 She stomped back across the patio, then sort of drifted into the darkness of Vigram\u8217\'92s house.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s legs were sweating fiercely now. He knew he should run, if only because these people were taking up far too much of his time with some nonsense. \u8220\'93Please,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93Just pay me what I\u8217\'92m owed, and I\u8217\'92ll be on my way.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93What precisely do you believe you are owed?}{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93A quarter silver string?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You are owed quite a bit more than that.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s commanding voice boomed out of the house. \u8220\'93Tomorrow!\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93If you }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 recall}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 , I am required elsewhere to-day!\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ah,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. He returned his attention to Mandri. \u8220\'93Tomorrow, then.\u8221\'94 He reached into his robe\u8217\'92s pocket. He pulled out a quarter string of silver, then dropped it into Mandri\u8217\'92s cupped hand. \u8220\'93I want to see you here tomorrow morning. I can promise you an opportunity which will give you everything that you ever wanted. I should add, you will not have to work for it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sure,\u8221\'94 Mandri mumbled as he fingered the short stack of silver coins. He did not count them, just felt their weight. He wasn\u8217\'92t interested in lingering any longer than he needed to. He wasn\u8217\'92t interested in returning any time soon. Definitely not tomorrow. He had plans for tomorrow.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He hurried down the patio\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s steps, refusing to return Vigram\u8217\'92s parting nod.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Look happier!\u8221\'94 Vigram called. \u8220\'93You should be excited!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri gave a polite smile over his shoulder, then hurried down Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s lane, which was the most terrifying lane because it was sandwiched between two leech lakes.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri kept to the right. The lake on the left held leeches bigger than his arm. Instead of stalls penning in live animals, its banks were lined with bones. The lake\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s center was a constant swirl as hundreds of leeches swarmed just under the water\u8217\'92s surface, bunch-crawling like caterpillars, slithering like eels, desperate to get in a taste of whatever corpse had bothered to drop in. Mandri grimaced at the sight of it. Then, suddenly, a round shape popped out of that writhing mass like a buoy. It rotated around, revealing itself to be a severed head, somewhat fresh, a human head, complete with close cropped hair, an upturned nose, and an open mouth which could not scream. A leech latched onto its cheek, and as soon as that had come, it sank.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nope!\u8221\'94 Mandri said to himself. \u8220\'93Nope, nope, nope,\u8221\'94 he repeated as he darted towards Vigram\u8217\'92s gate. Once onto the road, he quickened his pace. He didn\u8217\'92t feel out of reach until he crested the big hill that overlooked Vigram\u8217\'92s estate. Only then did he risk a look back.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram, still on his patio, stared straight through the distance, right at Mandri. The burly man cupped his voice and shouted, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Fate, boy! Fate!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri pretended not to hear.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He walked all the way to Geem\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s and used his pay to buy half a bushel of burgeons. They were down-valley burgeons, decent stuff, but the waxy capsule leaves were liable to split. The insides would dry out before he could get to them in the ways that he wanted to. But, that was all Geem had, so he bought them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He continued along the road, stomping his way through the muddy wheel-ruts, slapping away the flies, humming nursery rhymes, trying anything to distract himself from overthinking the sight of that severed head. Because it was only a severed head. That\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s all it was! It might have never belonged to a body, or been a person. There\u8217\'92s no way of knowing, really. Anything was possible. Besides, a rich man like Vigram was sure to accumulate enemies alongside the rest of his possessions. What was one little head?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri thought about his barren farm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about relaxing under his tree.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about sipping a milky hooch spiked through with burgeon juice.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He would like to escape into that hooch. It would be bliss.}
