\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 2.) }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Lora moaned. \u8220\'93Your assurances are always cheap. There is only what he }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 is,}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  and what he is }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 not}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 .\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93This all depresses me,\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he returned to his painting. His charcoal under drawing was bleeding pus. \u8220\'93I require a break. You two\u8230\'85why don\u8217\'92t you two clean up for now.\u8221\'94 He wiped his charcoal-stained fingers on an untouched corner of the canvas, then plodded off.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram, you can\u8217\'92t stop now,\u8221\'94 Mandri said after him. \u8220\'93If you give up in the middle of a failing work, you\u8217\'92ll make a bad habit.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll return. You two\u8230\'85you two get along.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram winked at Lora, then smiled wide. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m going to go pick out some wine. Something with a sweet bouquet.\u8221\'94 As soon as he announced he was leaving, he was gone.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram looked at the open hand. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93This was Fate, yes? It must be. You and he were to kiss, and then the ox\u8230\'85Here I was, wanting it caged!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 "Not every interruption is a scheme of Fate,\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Lora sneered. All the girlish charm in her voice was gone. Stern and measured, she stood up and fixed her hair. She scowled at Mandri\u8217\'92s demanding hand. \u8220\'93The boy is not as you described,\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93He is not }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 empty}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 . He attempted to }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 save}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  himself from injury.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What, because he dodged the ox\u8217\'92s charge?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked. \u8220\'93I addressed this before\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 we should not mistake any acts of self-preservation on his part for vitality. He is as broken as the rest of them, I assure you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri is on the balance beam}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Falls off}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora is like, you fucked up}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigrams like, whats wrong}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram expresses he could have sworn mandri was perfectly depressed}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora expresses shut the fuck up, he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s not it. He\u8217\'92s still got a spark. But this can be cured with death}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 OX crashes into the scene. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Coins spill}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri takes and flees.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Sees dead body. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Nope nope nope.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He was seduced.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 That\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s not possible.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 You doubt me?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Look at him! He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s barely here. He\u8217\'92s dead inside.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora is testing to see if Mandri has latent desire.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 If not, if he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s truly empty, she has found good material.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram!\u8221\'94 she shouted as she pushed him away. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stormed back out onto the patio, wine bottle in hand.  His eyes darted between Lora Mandri, puzzling out the reason for the awkward distance between them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora side-eyed Vigram with contempt. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He failed,\u8221\'94 she said curtly.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s shoulders sank. \u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s not possible,\u8221\'94 he argued. \u8220\'93Look at him!\u8221\'94 He pointed his wine bottle at Mandri. \u8220\'93He\u8217\'92s as empty inside as any young man we\u8217\'92ll ever find. What did he do? Did he kiss you? That could mean anything!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He was seduced, Vigram. You know what that means.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It could mean a number of things!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m sorry,\u8221\'94 Mandri interjected. \u8220\'93What is happening?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Both Lora and Vigram stared at him as though they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d just heard a rock speak.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, do you }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 feel}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  something for this girl?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I feel confused.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You see!\u8221\'94 Vigram exclaimed. \u8220\'93Sheer confusion is explanation enough. It might have been a confused reflex, an instinct. You ended the test too soon.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You doubt me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lump in Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s throat. \u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93No, of course not. I\u8217\'92m only upset I have to keep looking.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Alright, if you could pay me, I\u8217\'92m going to go ahead and leave.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m very sorry, Mandri. I\u8217\'92m sorry. You\u8217\'92re not what we\u8217\'92re looking for.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re going to stiff me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93In a manner of speaking, yes.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri got to his feet and brushed the dirt off the skirt of his robe. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m leaving,\u8221\'94 he said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You are not allowed to leave!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted. \u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re not finished!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Let the boy go,\u8221\'94 Lora sighed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Let him go? But we aren\u8217\'92t finished.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I think that fate has decided that we are. This was not meant to be.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Fate?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked, suddenly forgetting his rage. \u8220\'93You mean to say\u8230\'85\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I do,\u8221\'94 Lora answered. She eyed Vigram coldly, as if to shush him up. \u8220\'93This was not meant to be. Pay the boy his money.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hold on,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93Was all of this an attempt to get me and her together?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Pay him,\u8221\'94 Lora repeated.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93And why does that need to be said?\u8221\'94 Mandri wondered. \u8220\'93Were you were going to stiff me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram reached into his robe\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s pocket. \u8220\'93In a manner of speaking, yes. But, things being as they are, here is your payment.\u8221\'94 He pulled out a quarter string of silver, then dropped it into Mandri\u8217\'92s cupped hand. \u8220\'93Until we meet again.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He probably would have given in if his gaze hadn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t poked through the trellis behind her. In between the diamond gaps of wood and leafy vine, he glimpsed a giant yellow-headed ox hurtling towards them both. The lower half of its body was covered in swinging leeches.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He shoved Lora out of the way. He dived aside himself. The old ox, sagging spine and all, rammed right through the trellis. It stumbled onto the patio. Dewlap flapping, it crashed into Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s easel. Several foot long leeches flew through the air.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93MRRRRUUUUUUUUUU!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The Ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s wheeling hooves scratched and slipped on the brick. After a moment of chaos, it steadied itself, legs wide like a water bug.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Its snout was only three feet away from Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s face. Its protuberant eyes stared down at him as though it knew him. It snorted. It mooed. I was saying }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 something,}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  only Mandri could not interpret it. Seeing Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s confusion, the beast bucked and stumbled into the opposite side of the patio trellis, scrapping a few more leeches off its haunches before bursting through.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stormed back out onto the patio, wine bottle in hand. The ruin of his trellis stopped him in his tracks. His eyes darted between Lora, Mandri, and his abandoned painting, which lay face down on the dirty brick. Two little leeches were tossed upon it like two little wiggling turds.}
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She was Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s favorite subject, and the only child willing to sit for him. She was also unmarried. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Isn\u8217\'92t she a subject fit for holy oils?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked,  squeezing out a suggestive smile.}
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Undoubtedly,\u8221\'94 Mandri said as his eyes flicked again to Lora, without intention.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora was good natured, comely, with clear brown skin, sun-kissed cheeks.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri, this is Lora, my niece.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Your neice? You don't have a niece. You don't have any family.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 I lied.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 You lied about having a niece? Do you have a brother? Sister?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Move past it, Mandri. This is Lora.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Nice to meet you. = suggestive smile.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 ---What is going on here?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He seems disturbed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 By your beauty, I'd say. Mandri, help Lora up onto the stool.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 --}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 sees ox, etc.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 powers of observation}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 "What happened!?"}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 "The Ox interfered."}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 potentially move the ox interference down to being what frees Mandri.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 so like:}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 "Vigram! }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 "What?"}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 "He failed the test."}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 "He's food."}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 "I thought he was}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 -- throw this man into the brig?}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It can't be him. He ran away.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Fate, Vigram. Fate intervened. And anywyas, he ran away here. Absolutely no thought given to his self preservation}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 That's because he's an addict. He can't think.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  Many a man would leap at the chance, but Mandri averted his eyes. In doing so, he found himself staring into into the wild eye of an old yellow headed ox that was stuck in the nearest stall of the nearest leech lake.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nice to meet you, Mandri,\u8221\'94 Pel said. Her voice was soft and clear. She extended her arm in greeting. Around her wrist, a thin gold chain choked the softest flesh that Mandri had ever seen. Indeed, her short frame carried such a clean distribution of fat that it seemed she was boneless, an articulated pillow. That she stood upright seemed impossible. How? The strength of the perfection of the feminine, perhaps, or else her tendons were attached to the giddiness of men. Her unworked hand melted around his own knobby claw.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri smiled, pulled back, and averted his eyes. Vigram stared at the girl like he was about to stamp a return on interest. Seeing that, Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s mind was made up: there was no possible world in which Vigram and Pel were related. Why they were pretending was a mystery.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s too expensive,\u8221\'94 Mandri said instinctively. \u8220\'93Look at all this pigment. The canvas. It would take me weeks to afford all of this. Your uncle makes this in half a finger.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You could make that much too if you worked for him.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I do not want to do that.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1}